From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:39:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat: tab.new shell: false runs argv by itself, so its
 tab closes with it

tab.new runs an agent in your shell, which stays after the agent exits. A
program that is the whole tab (nvim-jay's Gerrit review) should take the tab
with it: shell: false spawns argv as is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
